[read-back] DANA: Taking those in order. "Never bid blind" means no inspection on a no-records machine or anything over $50,000. A fleet machine with records isn't really blind to me, because the records are the check.

The max bid is the hammer price. The $12,000 is a rough allowance for premium, freight and margin, not exact.

Without an inspection I use the lower of the two caps.

The $8,000 to $10,000 loss is the usual case. A $30,000 repair would lose more, and I haven't tracked that.

Two days is the minimum, and I don't remember the longest wait.

The "third" is just a rough feel.
